course: dictionary
lesson: 3535
title: February: the short month
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: February is a month, so it is a proper noun: it starts with a capital letter, like January and March. It is the second month of the year, after January and before March. «February has 28 days, or 29 in a leap year.» Count the days in the sentence to check the number.
explain: Read the clues around the word. «February is the shortest month» tells you it has fewer days than any other month. «All 12 months have at least 28 days; only February has just 28 (or 29 in a leap year).» So February is the odd one out, the only month with 28 or 29 days.
explain: The word can also tell you where in the world you are. In the UK, Ireland, Canada and the USA, February is in winter. In Australia and New Zealand, February is in summer. The same month can feel very different depending on where you live.
fact: February is the second month of the year.
fact: February has 28 days, or 29 in a leap year.
fact: February is the shortest month of the year.
fact: 28 days is exactly 4 weeks.
fact: A leap year comes every 4 years, because the Earth takes about 365 and a quarter days to go round the Sun, so an extra day is added to February.
exercise: «February has 28 days, or 29 in a leap year.» How many days does February have in a normal year? | *28 | 30 | 31 | 26
exercise: Nina says February is the longest month. Is she right? | No, it is the middle month of the year | Yes, it has 40 days | Yes, it has the most days | *No, February is the shortest month
exercise: In which season is February in the UK? | *Winter | Summer | Spring | Autumn
test: Which month comes just before March? | December | April | *February | January
test: How many days does February have in a leap year? | 28 | 30 | 27 | *29
exam: Waitangi Day is on 6 February in New Zealand; in a leap year, how many days come after 6 February in that month? | 24 | 6 | 22 | *23
